faq:
  - q: "What is Deloitte's hiring process in 2026?"
    a: "Deloitte's hiring process varies by service line (Consulting, Audit, Tax, Advisory, Risk) but follows a general pattern: (1) Online application and resume screen. (2) HireVue video interview — pre-recorded behavioral questions for most roles. (3) Aptitude and cognitive assessments — numerical reasoning, verbal, situational judgment (used for many campus hires). (4) First-round interviews with associates or managers — behavioral and role-specific. (5) Final-round partner or managing director interviews — combination of behavioral, case (for consulting roles), and leadership fit. The total process runs 4–8 weeks for campus hires and 6–10 weeks for experienced lateral hires. Deloitte hires at extremely high volume compared to MBB — selectivity is real but the process is less brutal than McKinsey or BCG."
  - q: "What does Deloitte look for in candidates?"
    a: "Deloitte evaluates candidates across four dimensions: (1) Analytical capability — structured problem solving, quantitative reasoning, and comfort with data and ambiguity. (2) Client impact orientation — candidates who frame their experiences in terms of outcomes delivered for others (clients, stakeholders, colleagues) consistently outperform. (3) Collaborative leadership — Deloitte's projects are team-delivered; candidates who demonstrate both individual contribution and team leadership are preferred. (4) Adaptability — Deloitte works across industries, functions, and geographies. The ability to context-switch, learn quickly, and apply frameworks across different client environments is a core signal."
  - q: "Does Deloitte Consulting use case interviews?"
    a: "Yes — Deloitte Consulting interviews include case interviews, but they are different from McKinsey or BCG cases. Deloitte uses both interviewer-led and candidate-led case formats depending on the office and recruiter. The cases tend to be less rigorous in structure and more discussion-based — they test problem decomposition, hypothesis-driven thinking, and basic quantitative reasoning rather than the deep analytical drilling of MBB interviews. For strategy and monitor roles, the case standard is higher. For federal consulting and implementation roles, behavioral interviews dominate over cases. Always confirm the format with your recruiter before preparing."
  - q: "How does Deloitte federal consulting recruiting work?"
    a: "Deloitte Government & Public Services (GPS) is one of the largest federal consulting practices in the US. Recruiting is distinct from commercial consulting: (1) Security clearance is often required or preferred — candidates with active Secret or TS/SCI clearances have a significant advantage. (2) Target schools include many second-tier and regional universities in addition to elite targets — GPS recruiting is broader than commercial. (3) Technical roles (data, cyber, cloud) have a higher technical bar and may include coding or architecture assessments. (4) Mission orientation matters — candidates who can articulate genuine interest in federal missions (defense, healthcare, tax administration) perform better than those solely motivated by compensation."
  - q: "What does Deloitte pay in 2026?"
    a: "Deloitte compensation varies significantly by service line. Consulting — Business Analyst (undergrad): $80–95K base + signing + performance bonus, total $90–110K. Consultant (post-MBA): $175–190K base + bonus, total $200–230K. Senior Consultant: $130–170K base. Manager: $160–220K base + bonus. Senior Manager: $200–280K total. Partner track is long (10–15 years) but equity is significant. Audit and Tax compensation is lower: $55–75K for staff; $80–110K for senior; $120–160K for manager. Advisory and risk roles fall between consulting and audit. Deloitte's comp is meaningfully below MBB and below FAANG engineering but competitive within Big Four."
  - q: "What is the Deloitte interview process for experienced hires?"
    a: "Experienced hire recruiting at Deloitte follows a targeted process: (1) Application or recruiter outreach via LinkedIn (Deloitte recruiters are active on LinkedIn for specialist roles). (2) Recruiter screen — 30 minutes on background, compensation expectations, and practice area fit. (3) Hiring manager interview — behavioral depth on relevant client experience and functional expertise. (4) Panel interview with 2–4 team members, senior manager, or partner — behavioral stories, domain knowledge, and client scenario questions. For technology and cyber roles, a technical assessment may be included. Experienced hires are evaluated heavily on client-facing impact and the depth of their industry or functional expertise rather than academic credentials."
